!! Composition
* 讠 from 言 (yán, speech) — semantic component
* 吾 (wú) — historically phonetic component; modern pronunciations no longer match closely

The traditional form is 語 (yǔ). In 中文 (Zhōngwén), 文 (wén) emphasizes writing/language; 汉语 (Hànyǔ) is another standard term for Chinese.

